From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:14:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 066/148] hjviewer: the PC home and the connect page around the
 gate

U16: the desktop home's left pane scrolls. Its scroll view is bounded
(Expanded) instead of sitting over an empty Expanded, so a pane taller
than the window, such as P1 over the install card of a PC that is not
installed, scrolls with the theme's thin bar and [Install] stays
reachable; _childKey and the incoming-only sizing are unchanged. The
main window cannot be made smaller than 720x520 (not the incoming-only
window).

U05: the PC home's notices fit the 200 px pane. A title over a text
takes one line with an ellipsis and the whole title in a tooltip; the
buttons are stacked at full width, 34 px high. G2 is a neutral outlined
box instead of a blue one that read as one with the ID's card. While P1
shows, the ID's card is a plain card, the ID and the one-time password
are dimmed, desk_tip says this PC cannot accept connections now, and a
PC without a login gets a line on the ID's card that logging in or the
access password makes the ID work. The text stays 12 px: P1's text
never fits two lines in the pane, so the 13 px variant would not show.

U04: one filled [Log in] per window. While P1 of a PC without a login or
G2 shows its filled [Log in], G3 keeps its text without a button and
the placeholder of a tab that needs a login shows a plain [Log in];
otherwise G3's [Log in] is plain and the placeholder's filled. G3 is one
line, "Staff-only server - Login required", with the whole hint in its
tooltip (a tap on phones). No side placement and no remembered
collapse, as decided for 1.8.2.

U08: on a phone, G3 is a card with a border, since the fill it had does
not show on the home's light canvas; the desktop keeps the fill on its
white pane.

U41: the card of a Windows PC that runs without being installed takes
the app's look, an info notice with one primary [Install], instead of
upstream's gradient card, and install_tip says why to install: it
starts with Windows, a login puts the PC in My PCs for unattended
connections, and UAC windows can be handled remotely. The notice after
a login there offers [Install] next to [OK].

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
